  "prediction": "**$8.2 Billion Merger: IntercontinentalExchange to Acquire New York Stock Exchange**\n\nIn a significant move that marks a shift in the global market for derivatives, IntercontinentalExchange (ICE) is set to acquire the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) in an $8.2 billion takeover. The deal, which is expected to be announced as early as Thursday morning, would see ICE offer approximately $33 a share, with two-thirds of that in stock, representing a 37% premium to NYSE Euronext's closing stock price on Wednesday.\n\nThe acquisition would link NYSE Euronext to one of the industry's fastest-growing exchanges, ICE, which has some of the highest profit margins in the business. The deal would also expand ICE's operations, which currently have around 1,000 employees, to include NYSE Euronext's 3,077 employees.\n\nThe merger marks a significant shift in the global market for derivatives, with the trading of stocks becoming a less attractive business. The New York Stock Exchange is now responsible for only about 11% of all stock trading, while NYSE Euronext's electronic Arca platform accounts for another 12%. In contrast, the trading of futures and options, where ICE is focused, has seen a decline in volume, but less than in stocks.\n\nThe acquisition would also seal the triumph of electronic trading over \"open outcry\" floor trading that long dominated financial markets. The deal would create a combined company that would own 14 stock and futures exchanges and five clearing operations, making it the largest player in the industry.\n\nRegulatory approval and shareholder approval are still required for the deal to go through. However, the acquisition is expected to face fewer antitrust concerns than previous proposed mergers, as ICE focuses on commodities like oil, natural gas, and cotton, while NYSE Euronext plies mainly in stock and stock options and derivatives.\n\nThe deal has been welcomed by investors, with shares of NYSE Euronext rising more than 21% in after-hours trading to $29.20. The acquisition is expected to bring significant benefits to both companies, including greater scale and cost savings, as well as access to new markets and customers.\n\nOverall, the $8.2 billion merger between ICE and NYSE Euronext marks a significant shift in the global market for derivatives and is expected to create a dominant player in the industry.",
